		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="9064"></a><b>Nimui</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Magically Delicious<br /><img src="images/Ranks/swords/3sword.gif" alt="Journeyman" title="Journeyman" border="0" /><br /><img src="images/avatars/gallery/general/luckycharms.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Joined: 22 Aug 2002<br />Posts: 129<br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=9064&amp;sid=8da7eee9e483275c339e2eb04e08b84c#9064"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Wed Jan 09, 2002 8:19 am<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=9064&amp;sid=8da7eee9e483275c339e2eb04e08b84c"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">I was born and raised in the lofty tree city of Kelethin.  When I was small I wasn’t supposed to descend from the heights.  But, being as curious as I am, I snuck down one day when me mum wasn’t looking and promptly tracked a spiderling away from the lift.  Much to my surprise, the spider turned on me and started attacking me.  So I pulled my tiny dagger from my belt and began to fight back.  It seemed like forever that we battled, before the spiderling turned to flee and I was able to slay it.  Feeling aglow with the victory I looked down at myself and my thoughts immediately turned apprehensive.  I had spider bites and spider blood and gore all over my freshly cleaned shirt.  “Ut oh, me mum is gonna tan my hide,” I said to myself.  Resigning myself to being grounded for life, I grabbed the spiderling silk, ran back and caught the lift up to city.  
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
I crept back to my home and almost cried with relief when I saw me mum wasn’t in the kitchen.  I walked quietly towards my room hoping to make it without being caught, but alas, my fa came out of his room.  “Come here Nimui,” he said sternly.  I walked over to him, holding my head high to show no fear.  “Tis a good thing you are home now.  I was just about to set out hunting for you,” he said and continued, “Yer mum found out ye were gone.”   He then stopped and took a good look at me and realized my disheveled appearance.  “Where have you been?” he cried.  “I went down the lift, Fa.  I only wanted to feel the grass under my feet,” I whispered shamefaced. “And then I saw a little spiderling so I followed it,” I continued, “but I didn’t know it would turn on me.  It was biting me and it hurt, so I had to fight it.  I know I am to respect all of Tunare’s creatures but it was hurting me.  I slew it and took this silken thing from it.”  I hand over the silk to my fa.  “ I’m sorry,” I mumble.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Then to my utter shock, my fa begins to laugh.  “Well lass, it seems as if you have a bit of yer old man in ye,” he laughed.  “I too snuck down when I wasn’t supposed to and made my first kill of one the little buggers,” he continued “and nay, don’t worry, it wasn’t one of Tunare’s creatures.   Are ye hurt though?”  I shook my head no, and showed him twas only a few bites.  He reached into his pouch and rubbed some salve on my bites to help them heal faster.  “Well then, tis time to take you to the Rangers guild.  If you’re going to hunt, you need to learn from the masters” he said.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Thus, I began my training as a Ranger and have learnt much  already of hunting and surviving in Tunare’s lands.  
<br />

<br />
 
<br />
